  // StableHLO convolution expects kernel shape (out_channels, in_channels/groups, kD, kH, kW)
  // So we need to reverse the first two dims of the kernel.
  //
  // Steps:
  // 1) Reverse the first two dims of %arg0 to get kernel with shape [7,6,3,3,3]
  // 2) Use stablehlo.convolution with:
  //    lhs = %arg1 (input) shape [8,6,8,8,8]
  //    rhs = reversed kernel [7,6,3,3,3]
  //    dimension_numbers = #stablehlo.conv<[b, f, 0, 1, 2]x[o, i, 0, 1, 2]->[b, f, 0, 1, 2]>
  //    lhs_dilation = [1,1,1] (stride of transposed conv)
  //    rhs_dilation = [1,1,1] (kernel dilation)
  //    window_strides = [1,1,1] (stride of convolution)
  //    padding = [[0,0],[0,0],[0,0]] (no padding)
  //    feature_group_count = 1
  //
