  // Define window dimensions: kernel=16, stride=16, no padding
  // Reduce window over dimension 1 (width dimension)
  // The window dims correspond to the last dimension (width=1), but kernel=16 > 1 is invalid.
  // Actually, the input width is 1, but kernel=16, so the input width must be >=16.
  // The input width is 1, so the pooling is over the feature dimension (16).
  // In PyTorch, AvgPool1d is applied over the last dimension (width).
  // Here, the input to AvgPool1d is (batch=16, channels=16, width=1)
  // But in the code, x.unsqueeze(1) makes shape (16,1,16), not (16,16,1).
  // Correction: unsqueeze(1) inserts dimension at position 1, so shape is (16,1,16)
