  // ConvTranspose3d is implemented as a convolution with lhs_dilation = stride, padding adjusted, and output_padding
  // Given stride=2, padding=1, output_padding=1, kernel=3
  // The conv_transpose.weight shape is (6,7,3,3,3) (in_channels=6, out_channels=7)
  // StableHLO convolution expects kernel shape (out_channels, in_channels, ...), so we need to transpose weight dims from (6,7,3,3,3) to (7,6,3,3,3)
  // But the input weight is (6,7,3,3,3), so we must transpose first two dims

  // Transpose weight from (6,7,3,3,3) to (7,6,3,3,3)
  %weight_transposed = stablehlo.transpose %arg1 : tensor<6x7x3x3x3xf32> to tensor<7x6x3x3x3xf32> {permutation = [1,0,2,3,4]}

