  //
  // The convolution above yields 5x4 output spatial dims, so we must set lhs_dilation = stride = 1,
  // but the input spatial dims are 7x8, kernel 3x5, so output spatial dims:
  // (7-1)*1 - 0 + 1*(3-1) + 0 + 1 = 9 (height)
  // (8-1)*1 - 0 + 1*(5-1) + 0 + 1 = 12 (width)
  //
  // So the convolution op must be called with lhs_dilation = stride = (1,1)
  // and padding = 0, output_padding = 0
  //
  // The convolution op expects lhs_dilation attribute to be array<i64: 1, 1>
  //
  // So redo convolution with lhs_dilation = stride = (1,1)
  // The previous convolution used lhs_dilation=1, so it is correct.
  //
  // The output shape from convolution is 6x7x9x12, as required.
  //
  // So the previous convolution op call is incorrect in output shape comment.
  //
  // We must fix the convolution op call to have lhs_dilation = stride = (1,1)
  // and padding = 0, output_padding = 0
  //
  // The convolution op call above is correct, but the output shape in comment was wrong.
  //
  // So the convolution op call produces tensor<6x7x9x12xf32> as required.

