  // lhs = input tensor, shape [6, 6, 7, 8]
  // rhs = weight tensor, shape [7, 6, 3, 5]
  // But stablehlo.convolution expects rhs kernel shape [out_channels, in_channels/groups, ...]
  // For ConvTranspose2d, the weight shape is [in_channels, out_channels, kernel_h, kernel_w]
  // So we need to reverse the roles of in/out channels in the kernel:
  // We must reverse the kernel dims 0 and 1 to get [out_channels, in_channels, kernel_h, kernel_w]
  // The input is [batch, in_channels, H, W]
  // The output is [batch, out_channels, H_out, W_out]

  // Step 1: Reverse the first two dimensions of the kernel to get [7,6,3,5]
  // stablehlo.reverse can only reverse along dimensions, but we want to transpose dims 0 and 1.
  // So we do a transpose instead by reshaping and permuting dims.

  // Implement transpose of kernel from [6,7,3,5] to [7,6,3,5]
