  // Actually, stablehlo does not have a direct transpose op, so we use broadcast_in_dim + reshape trick:
  // But better to do a reshape + transpose via reshape + stablehlo.transpose (not in ops)
  // Since stablehlo does not have transpose op, we do a reshape + stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim + reshape trick:
  // Instead, we do a reshape + stablehlo.reshape + stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim + stablehlo.reshape is complicated.
  // The simplest is to use stablehlo.convolution dimension_numbers to swap lhs and rhs dims accordingly.
  // So we keep weight as is and set dimension_numbers accordingly.

  // Convolution dimension numbers:
  // lhs: batch, in_channels, height, width = [16,6,8,8]
  // rhs: out_channels, in_channels, kernel_h, kernel_w = [7,6,3,3]
  // Our weight is [6,7,3,3], so we need to transpose first two dims.
  // We do a reshape + stablehlo.reshape + stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim + stablehlo.reshape to transpose dims 0 and 1:
  // Reshape to 6 x 7 x 3 x 3 -> 6 x 7 x 9
